# =====================================================================================
# reducts.ttl — the forgetful reduct / theory-morphism edges + obligation-counting
# extension morphisms of the folded algebra spine (W2 · SP0, T-REDUCT). Stage 2.
# =====================================================================================
# D24 A6: the tower is theories + model-classes + REDUCTS (forgetful theory-morphisms),
# NOT a subclass ladder of witness-defined classes. This file mints the seven forgetful
# reduct edges child->parent as rec:reduct:record individuals (records.ttl:86-90, one
# cardinality-1 @rel:reduct restriction each) and the THREE obligation-counting extension
# morphisms for the two-sided laws (monoid identity, group inverse, loop identity) so a
# rung declaring only ONE side of a two-sided law is RED (design §1.6, §1.9, §3).
#
# THE SEVEN REDUCT EDGES (design §1.9; child forgets structure -> parent theory):
#   semigroup->magma       (forgets associativity)      obligation-count 1
#   monoid->semigroup      (forgets the two-sided identity)   obligation-count 2  [ext]
#   commutative:monoid->monoid (forgets commutativity)  obligation-count 1
#   group->monoid          (forgets the two-sided inverse)    obligation-count 2  [ext]
#   abelian:group->group   (forgets commutativity)      obligation-count 1
#   quasigroup->magma      (forgets latin-division)      obligation-count 1
#   loop->quasigroup       (forgets the two-sided identity)   obligation-count 2  [ext]
# magma->progenitor is rdfs:subClassOf (spine/magma.ttl), NOT a reduct — the progenitor
# grounds nothing, so there is no theory to forget TO (design §1.9, §3).
#
# ONE LAW = ONE OBLIGATION-COUNT-BEARING EDGE. Each reduct carries @rel:adds:law -> the
# SINGLE law the child adds over its parent (re-homing fnd:addsLaw, algebra_spine.ttl:99-103
# — Directive-17 one-law-per-child, constraint B no-cram + constraint C at-least-one) plus
# an @rel:obligation:count. probes/one_law_per_rung.rq reddens any reduct whose @rel:adds:law
# count != 1 (both bounds together). A single LAW may discharge TWO OBLIGATIONS: the two-sided
# identity/inverse is ONE added law but TWO equation records (left + right, design §1.6, §3),
# so its reduct carries obligation-count 2 and an EXTENSION MORPHISM.
#
# THE THREE EXTENSION MORPHISMS (design §1.6). Each two-sided reduct @rel:extension -> an
# obligation-counting extension morphism (kingdom:mapping…class:extension…genus:obligation:
# species:count:two) that reifies the two obligation slots of the two-sided law as an ordered
# pair: @rel:left -> the left-side equation record, @rel:right -> the right-side equation record,
# @rel:obligation:count 2. It is dual-typed rec:equation:record — the SAME dual-typing precedent
# equations.ttl:57-58 uses for associativity (rec:axiom:record + rec:equation:record) — so the
# GENERIC EquationRecordShape (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl:119-135, cardinality-1 @rel:left AND
# @rel:right; the design earmarks it "two-sided = 2 records", plan T-SHAPES) is REUSED as the
# biting SHACL tooth: an extension morphism that carries only ONE side (a rung declaring only
# identity-left, say) drops below minCount-1 on the missing side and EquationRecordShape flips
# conforms True->False, WITHOUT a new shape. probes/obligation_count.rq is the parallel probe
# tooth (a count-two obligation missing a side -> >=1 row).
#
# NAMING (D26 LOCKED). Full mathematics 12-marker ladder under HEAD (alg:); reduct edges
# kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:
# species:<child>:to:<parent>:component:definition:instance:canonical; extension morphisms
# kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:<rung>:genus:
# obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical. Compound children are
# adjective-FIRST (B1 LOCKED §7.2 #9): commutative:monoid / abelian:group. [S] = no runtime
# precedent -> §7.2 sign-off packet (block at the foot).
#
# Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md (§1.6, §1.9, §3, §7.2 #4).
# Plan:   docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-spine-fold-plan.md (T-REDUCT).
# Consumes (do not rewrite): records.ttl (rec:reduct:record, rec:equation:record), the 8 rung
# theory atoms (spine/*.ttl, the @rel:reduct parent targets + the two-sided side equation records),
# equations.ttl (monoid identity-left/right). Tooth: shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl EquationRecordShape
# (over the extension morphisms) + probes/one_law_per_rung.rq + probes/obligation_count.rq.

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
# mathematics 12-marker ladder head (D26), ending at subdomain: (records.ttl / spine idiom):
@prefix alg:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:domain:mathematics:realm:algebra:subdomain:> .
# consolidated relation namespace (@rel = @P:relation; records.ttl:41):
@prefix rel:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:> .
# seed-carrier record-class ladder (records.ttl:38-39) — rec:reduct:record / rec:equation:record REUSED:
@prefix rec:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:grounding:ontology:basic:formal:domain:knowledge:representation:kingdom:specification:phylum:formal:contract:class:class:order:declared:family:seed:genus:registry:species:> .

# =====================================================================================
# 1. THE SEVEN FORGETFUL REDUCT EDGES (rec:reduct:record; design §1.9). @rel:reduct -> the
#    parent THEORY the morphism forgets to (byte-identical to the child theory's own @rel:reduct,
#    spine/*.ttl); @rel:adds:law -> the SINGLE law the child adds over the parent (one-law-per-child);
#    @rel:obligation:count -> the number of equation-record obligations that law discharges (1, or 2
#    for a two-sided law). Provenance quartet + @rel:authority "SYN" on every RECORD (honesty ledger:
#    the reduct/extension-morphism machinery is synthesized tower structure, exactly as fnd:addsLaw was
#    SYN, algebra_spine.ttl:101) — never on a mathematical denotatum.
# =====================================================================================

# --- semigroup -> magma (forgets associativity; 1 obligation) ---
alg:semigroup:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:semigroup:to:magma:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct semigroup -> magma" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: semigroup |-> magma (forgets associativity)" ;
    rel:reduct   alg:magma:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:magma:genus:presented:species:magma:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law alg:semigroup:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:associativity:order:binary:family:semigroup:genus:composition:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism semigroup |-> magma (D24 A6, design §1.9): the reduct that FORGETS associativity, leaving the bare magma theory (Sigma={·}, E={closure}). Typed rec:reduct:record (records.ttl:86-90, cardinality-1 @rel:reduct restriction); @rel:reduct points at the magma theory atom (byte-identical to spine/semigroup.ttl:87's own @rel:reduct). @rel:adds:law -> the SINGLE law semigroup adds over magma (associativity; re-homing fnd:addsLaw, algebra_spine.ttl:99-103 one-law-per-child, constraints B no-cram + C at-least-one, made a graph fact by probes/one_law_per_rung.rq). @rel:obligation:count 1: associativity is ONE equation (not two-sided, design §1.6), so it discharges exactly one equation-record obligation and needs NO extension morphism. [S] order:forgetful (§7.2 #4) and genus:theory (§7.2 #4) are UNATTESTED in the runtime -> maintainer sign-off packet. Provenance quartet + @rel:authority SYN on this RECORD (synthesized tower machinery), never on a denotatum." .

# --- monoid -> semigroup (forgets the two-sided identity; 2 obligations -> extension morphism) ---
alg:monoid:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:monoid:to:semigroup:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct monoid -> semigroup" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: monoid |-> semigroup (forgets the two-sided identity)" ;
    rel:reduct    alg:semigroup:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:semigroup:genus:presented:species:semigroup:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law  alg:monoid:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:monoid:genus:neutral:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:extension alg:monoid:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:monoid:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism monoid |-> semigroup (design §1.9): the reduct that FORGETS the two-sided identity, leaving the semigroup theory. @rel:reduct -> the semigroup theory (byte-identical to spine/monoid.ttl:75). @rel:adds:law -> the ONE law monoid adds over semigroup (the two-sided identity parent axiom, monoid.ttl:133 — a SINGLE added law, one-law-per-child). @rel:obligation:count 2: that ONE two-sided law discharges TWO equation-record obligations (identity-left e·x=x AND identity-right x·e=x, equations.ttl:70-90, design §1.6 §3), so @rel:extension -> the obligation-counting extension morphism below, and probes/obligation_count.rq + the EquationRecordShape over that morphism redden a monoid that declares only ONE side. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4 sign-off. Provenance + @rel:authority SYN on the record." .

# --- commutative:monoid -> monoid (forgets commutativity; 1 obligation) ---
alg:commutative:monoid:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:commutative:monoid:to:monoid:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct commutative:monoid -> monoid" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: commutative monoid |-> monoid (forgets commutativity)" ;
    rel:reduct   alg:monoid:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:monoid:genus:presented:species:monoid:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law alg:commutative:monoid:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:commutativity:order:binary:family:commutative:monoid:genus:composition:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism commutative:monoid |-> monoid (design §1.9; compound child adjective-FIRST, B1 LOCKED §7.2 #9): the reduct that FORGETS commutativity, leaving the plain monoid theory. @rel:reduct -> the monoid theory (byte-identical to spine/commutative_monoid.ttl:101). @rel:adds:law -> the SINGLE law commutative:monoid adds over monoid (commutativity, its OWN atom off the compound subdomain — Directive-17 no-cram, distinct from the abelian:group commutativity atom, bridges.ttl:178-181). @rel:obligation:count 1: commutativity is ONE equation (not two-sided), no extension morphism. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4. Provenance + SYN on the record." .

# --- group -> monoid (forgets the two-sided inverse; 2 obligations -> extension morphism) ---
alg:group:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:group:to:monoid:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct group -> monoid" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: group |-> monoid (forgets the two-sided inverse)" ;
    rel:reduct    alg:monoid:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:monoid:genus:presented:species:monoid:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law  alg:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:inverse:order:binary:family:group:genus:member:species:inverse:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:extension alg:group:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:group:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism group |-> monoid (design §1.9): the reduct that FORGETS the two-sided inverse, leaving the monoid theory (the group descends from monoid, NOT from commutative:monoid — the spine forks here). @rel:reduct -> the monoid theory (byte-identical to spine/group.ttl:101). @rel:adds:law -> the ONE law group adds over monoid (the two-sided inverse parent axiom, group.ttl — a SINGLE added law). @rel:obligation:count 2: the two-sided inverse discharges TWO equation-record obligations (inverse-left x·inv(x)=e AND inverse-right inv(x)·x=e, spine/group.ttl:190-199, design §1.6), so @rel:extension -> the group inverse extension morphism below; a group declaring only one inverse side reddens. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4. Provenance + SYN on the record." .

# --- abelian:group -> group (forgets commutativity; 1 obligation) ---
alg:abelian:group:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:abelian:group:to:group:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct abelian:group -> group" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: abelian group |-> group (forgets commutativity)" ;
    rel:reduct   alg:group:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:group:genus:presented:species:group:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law alg:abelian:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:commutativity:order:binary:family:abelian:group:genus:composition:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism abelian:group |-> group (design §1.9; compound child adjective-FIRST, B1 LOCKED §7.2 #9): the reduct that FORGETS commutativity, leaving the plain group theory. @rel:reduct -> the group theory (byte-identical to spine/abelian_group.ttl:115). @rel:adds:law -> the SINGLE law abelian:group adds over group (commutativity, its OWN atom off the compound subdomain — the SAME law added at TWO spine points, commutative:monoid and abelian:group, each its own atom, no-cram, bridges.ttl:178-181). @rel:obligation:count 1: commutativity is ONE equation, no extension morphism. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4. Provenance + SYN on the record." .

# --- quasigroup -> magma (forgets latin-division; 1 obligation) ---
alg:quasigroup:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:quasigroup:to:magma:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct quasigroup -> magma" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: quasigroup |-> magma (forgets latin-division)" ;
    rel:reduct   alg:magma:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:magma:genus:presented:species:magma:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law alg:quasigroup:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:division:order:binary:family:quasigroup:genus:latin:species:unique:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism quasigroup |-> magma (design §1.9): the reduct that FORGETS unique latin-division, leaving the bare magma theory (the division sub-family descends from magma, NOT from semigroup — a quasigroup need not be associative). @rel:reduct -> the magma theory (byte-identical to spine/quasigroup.ttl:122). @rel:adds:law -> the SINGLE law quasigroup adds over magma (unique latin left/right division, ONE law of the quasigroup theory, spine/quasigroup.ttl). @rel:obligation:count 1: modelled as ONE equation record (the unique-division law is a single latin-square membership statement, design §1.9 / bridges.ttl:174), so no extension morphism. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4; the added law's genus:latin / species:unique are likewise [S] (§7.2 #5, flagged at bridges.ttl:174-175). Provenance + SYN on the record." .

# --- loop -> quasigroup (forgets the two-sided identity; 2 obligations -> extension morphism) ---
alg:loop:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:reduct:order:forgetful:family:morphism:genus:theory:species:loop:to:quasigroup:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:reduct:record ;
    rdfs:label "reduct loop -> quasigroup" ;
    rel:notation "forgetful reduct: loop |-> quasigroup (forgets the two-sided identity)" ;
    rel:reduct    alg:quasigroup:kingdom:definition:phylum:algebra:class:theory:order:declarative:family:quasigroup:genus:presented:species:quasigroup:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:adds:law  alg:loop:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:loop:genus:neutral:species:member:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:extension alg:loop:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:loop:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The forgetful theory-morphism loop |-> quasigroup (design §1.9): the reduct that FORGETS the two-sided identity, leaving the quasigroup theory. @rel:reduct -> the quasigroup theory (byte-identical to spine/loop.ttl:129). @rel:adds:law -> the ONE law loop adds over quasigroup (the two-sided identity, loop's OWN atom off the division sub-family — the SAME shape of law monoid adds, but a distinct atom, no-cram). @rel:obligation:count 2: the two-sided identity discharges TWO equation-record obligations (loop identity-left AND identity-right, spine/loop.ttl:224-234, design §1.6), so @rel:extension -> the loop identity extension morphism below; a loop declaring only one identity side reddens. [S] order:forgetful / genus:theory UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #4. Provenance + SYN on the record." .

# =====================================================================================
# 2. THE THREE OBLIGATION-COUNTING EXTENSION MORPHISMS (design §1.6, §3). One per two-sided
#    law (monoid identity, group inverse, loop identity). Each reifies the TWO obligation slots
#    of its two-sided law as an ordered pair: @rel:left -> the left-side equation record,
#    @rel:right -> the right-side equation record, @rel:obligation:count 2. DUAL-TYPED
#    rec:equation:record (the equations.ttl:57-58 associativity dual-typing precedent) so the
#    GENERIC EquationRecordShape (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl:119-135; cardinality-1 @rel:left AND
#    @rel:right) is REUSED as the biting tooth — an extension morphism missing a side flips
#    conforms True->False, WITHOUT a new shape (design earmarks EquationRecordShape "two-sided =
#    2 records", plan T-SHAPES). probes/obligation_count.rq is the parallel probe tooth.
# =====================================================================================

# --- monoid identity extension morphism (e·x=x AND x·e=x -> 2 obligations) ---
alg:monoid:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:monoid:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "monoid two-sided identity obligation (count 2)" ;
    rel:notation "monoid identity discharges 2 obligations: e·x=x (left) AND x·e=x (right)" ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:left  alg:monoid:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:monoid:genus:neutral:species:member:left:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:right alg:monoid:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:monoid:genus:neutral:species:member:right:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The obligation-counting EXTENSION MORPHISM of the monoid->semigroup reduct (design §1.6, §3): the two-sided identity is ONE added law but discharges TWO equation-record obligations, and this morphism COUNTS them (@rel:obligation:count 2) by naming both slots — @rel:left -> the identity-LEFT equation record (e·x=x, equations.ttl:70) and @rel:right -> the identity-RIGHT equation record (x·e=x, equations.ttl:83). It is dual-typed rec:equation:record (the SAME dual-typing precedent equations.ttl:57-58 uses for associativity = rec:axiom:record + rec:equation:record) so the GENERIC EquationRecordShape's cardinality-1 @rel:left AND @rel:right teeth (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl:119-135) apply to it directly: a monoid that declares only ONE side leaves this morphism missing a slot, EquationRecordShape flips conforms True->False, and probes/obligation_count.rq returns a row — WITHOUT authoring a new shape. [S] genus:obligation and species:count:two are UNATTESTED in the runtime (§7.2 #6), as is the mapping-atom / rec:equation:record dual-typing choice -> maintainer sign-off packet. The IRI rides kingdom:mapping (a morphism), the type rides rec:equation:record (the pair-shaped obligation it reifies)." .

# --- group inverse extension morphism (x·inv(x)=e AND inv(x)·x=e -> 2 obligations) ---
alg:group:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:group:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "group two-sided inverse obligation (count 2)" ;
    rel:notation "group inverse discharges 2 obligations: x·inv(x)=e (left) AND inv(x)·x=e (right)" ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:left  alg:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:inverse:order:binary:family:group:genus:member:species:inverse:left:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:right alg:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:inverse:order:binary:family:group:genus:member:species:inverse:right:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The obligation-counting EXTENSION MORPHISM of the group->monoid reduct (design §1.6, §3): the two-sided inverse is ONE added law discharging TWO equation-record obligations, counted here (@rel:obligation:count 2) by naming both slots — @rel:left -> the inverse-LEFT equation record (x·inv(x)=e, spine/group.ttl:190) and @rel:right -> the inverse-RIGHT equation record (inv(x)·x=e, spine/group.ttl:199). Dual-typed rec:equation:record (the equations.ttl:57-58 precedent) so the GENERIC EquationRecordShape cardinality-1 @rel:left AND @rel:right teeth bite: a group declaring only one inverse side leaves a slot empty, EquationRecordShape flips True->False, obligation_count.rq returns a row. [S] genus:obligation / species:count:two + the mapping / rec:equation:record dual-typing UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #6 sign-off." .

# --- loop identity extension morphism (e·x=x AND x·e=x -> 2 obligations) ---
alg:loop:kingdom:mapping:phylum:composition:class:extension:order:declarative:family:loop:genus:obligation:species:count:two:component:definition:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "loop two-sided identity obligation (count 2)" ;
    rel:notation "loop identity discharges 2 obligations: e·x=x (left) AND x·e=x (right)" ;
    rel:obligation:count "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:left  alg:loop:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:loop:genus:neutral:species:member:left:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:right alg:loop:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:identity:order:binary:family:loop:genus:neutral:species:member:right:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The obligation-counting EXTENSION MORPHISM of the loop->quasigroup reduct (design §1.6, §3): loop's two-sided identity is ONE added law discharging TWO equation-record obligations, counted here (@rel:obligation:count 2) by naming both slots — @rel:left -> the loop identity-LEFT equation record (e·x=x, spine/loop.ttl:224) and @rel:right -> the loop identity-RIGHT equation record (x·e=x, spine/loop.ttl:234). Dual-typed rec:equation:record (the equations.ttl:57-58 precedent) so the GENERIC EquationRecordShape cardinality-1 @rel:left AND @rel:right teeth bite: a loop declaring only one identity side leaves a slot empty, EquationRecordShape flips True->False, obligation_count.rq returns a row. [S] genus:obligation / species:count:two + the mapping / rec:equation:record dual-typing UNATTESTED -> §7.2 #6 sign-off." .

